#: web/templates/settings.html
msgid "What the test checks"
msgstr ""

#: web/templates/settings.html
msgid "Test of the reading model"
msgstr ""

#: web/templates/settings.html
msgid ""
"The test builds a small temporary wiki with two pages and asks three questions with the fields above. First: a "
"question the page answers, in the mode that retrieves before asking; the model must answer with the datum of the page"
" and cite the page. Second: a question the page does not answer; the model must say it found no answer. Third: the "
"first question in the mode with tools; the model must search the wiki before it answers. The test takes about ten "
"seconds and makes three calls to the model."
msgstr ""

#: web/templates/settings.html
msgid ""
"Limits. Passing is necessary, not sufficient: the test finds a model that cannot do the work, and it does not compare"
" two models that can. A model gives different answers in two runs: repeat a doubtful result. The temporary wiki is "
"deleted at the end, and your wiki is not read."
msgstr ""

#: web/templates/settings.html
msgid "Test of the ingestion model"
msgstr ""

#: web/templates/settings.html
msgid ""
"The test builds a small temporary wiki and ingests a text of one paragraph with the fields above, through the same "
"steps as a real ingestion. The model must write the summary page and at least one concept page that names the source,"
" and the review of the wiki must find no error. The test takes about twenty seconds and makes several calls to the "
"model."
msgstr ""

#: web/templates/settings.html
msgid ""
"Limits. Passing is necessary, not sufficient: one short text does not show how the model handles a long document. A "
"model gives different results in two runs: repeat a doubtful result. The temporary wiki is deleted at the end, and "
"your wiki is not changed."
msgstr ""

#: web/templates/settings.html
msgid "Test of the vision model"
msgstr ""

#: web/templates/settings.html
msgid ""
"The test sends one scanned page that ships with the product, with a text and a table that are invented. First: the "
"model reads the page as the OCR does; the fourteen data of the page (a code, dates, amounts, the cells of the table) "
"must be in what it reads. Second: the model describes the same page as an image, in the format the product asks for. "
"The test takes about ten seconds and makes two calls to the model."
msgstr ""

#: web/templates/settings.html
msgid ""
"Limits. Passing is necessary, not sufficient: the page is clean and printed, and a photograph or handwriting is "
"harder. A model gives different results in two runs: repeat a doubtful result. The test does not check Tesseract, "
